hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"984","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala al-San’ani and Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam al-Ijli narrated to us, who said: Mu’tamar narrated to us, Ahmad said, he said: I heard Mu’ammar, Muhammad said: On the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that He said: “Whoever performs two rak’ahs of the afternoon prayer before the sun sets or performs one rak’ah of the morning prayer before sunrise has performed.”"
